The Java code provided calculates the 10th Fibonacci number using a recursive approach. Below is the translation into Python, preserving the functionality and adapting to Python idioms (such as using a more standard function definition and print statement).

```python
def fib(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return n
    return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)

if __name__ == "__main__":
    print(fib(10))
```

